{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LwCnYwwkxnPJqVnCv6yoTB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils reimplements GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test a specification-driven code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: SRDs define utility behavior → cobbler orchestrator generates Go code in cmd/ and pkg/ → differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) verifies output parity against GNU binaries. Shared infrastructure in pkg/sys (syscalls), pkg/format (formatting), pkg/testutils (testing).\n\n**Current state**: 33 releases defined (00.0–15.0). Most releases have partial or full implementations. The `requirement_states` field shows only **release 15.0** (ts, stty, pr, ptx) has requirements in \"ready\" state. Recent commits completed srd004-ts R1.1–R1.4 and srd105-stty R1.1, so cmd/ts and cmd/stty already exist with initial code.\n\n**Current release**: 15.0 — complex utilities. All four use cases (ts, stty, pr, ptx) have code status \"not started\" per analysis, but recent commits show ts and stty have partial implementations.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nOnly requirements with status \"ready\" should get tasks. All ready requirements are in release 15.0:\n- **srd004-ts**: 28 ready requirements (R1.5–R10.3)\n- **srd105-stty**: 10 ready requirements (R2.1–R7.3)\n- **srd110-pr**: 9 ready requirements (R2.1–R5.2)\n- **srd111-ptx**: 8 ready requirements (R2.1–R5.2)\n\ncmd/ts and cmd/stty already exist (from recent commits). cmd/pr and cmd/ptx do not exist yet and would need contract tasks first. With a 4-task limit, continuing existing implementations (stty, ts) maximizes progress. Canonical ordering: stty before ts (alphabetical by file path).\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nWeights not provided in project_context; using default weight of 1 per requirement.\n\n```\nTask 0: srd105-stty R2.1 (w=1), R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1), R4.1 (w=1) → Total: 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd105-stty R5.1 (w=1), R6.1 (w=1), R6.2 (w=1), R7.1 (w=1) → Total: 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd004-ts R1.5 (w=1), R1.6 (w=1), R2.1 (w=1), R2.2 (w=1) → Total: 4 ✓\nTask 3: srd004-ts R2.3 (w=1), R2.4 (w=1), R3.1 (w=1), R3.2 (w=1) → Total: 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/stty implementation (srd105-stty R2.1, R3.1, R3.2, R4.1)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd105-stty.yaml (full SRD for stty utility -- read all requirements R2.1, R3.1, R3.2, R4.1)\n      - cmd/stty/main.go (existing implementation from srd105-stty R1.1)\n      - cmd/stty/stty_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel15.0-uc002-stty.yaml (use case for stty)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (sys package API for terminal operations)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/stty/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add features for srd105-stty R2.1, R3.1, R3.2, R4.1\n      - path: cmd/stty/stty_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for R2.1, R3.1, R3.2, R4.1\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd105-stty R2.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd105-stty R3.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd105-stty R3.2 per the SRD acceptance criteria\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd105-stty R4.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing cmd/stty implementation -- do not rewrite or restructure existing code from R1.1\n      - id: D2\n        text: Follow the differential testing pattern from pkg/testutils using RunDiffTests against the gstty reference binary\n      - id: D3\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per the SIGPIPE shared protocol\n      - id: D4\n        text: Use golang.org/x/sys/unix for termios operations per architecture technology choices\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/stty/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/stty/... -count=1 passes all tests including new ones for R2.1, R3.1, R3.2, R4.1\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/stty/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Each of the four requirements has at least one differential test case in stty_test.go\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/stty implementation (srd105-stty R5.1, R6.1, R6.2, R7.1)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd105-stty.yaml (full SRD for stty utility -- read all requirements R5.1, R6.1, R6.2, R7.1)\n      - cmd/stty/main.go (existing implementation including R1.1, R2.1, R3.1, R3.2, R4.1)\n      - cmd/stty/stty_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (sys package API for terminal operations)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/stty/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add features for srd105-stty R5.1, R6.1, R6.2, R7.1\n      - path: cmd/stty/stty_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for R5.1, R6.1, R6.2, R7.1\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd105-stty R5.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd105-stty R6.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd105-stty R6.2 per the SRD acceptance criteria\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd105-stty R7.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing cmd/stty implementation -- do not rewrite or restructure existing code\n      - id: D2\n        text: Follow the differential testing pattern from pkg/testutils using RunDiffTests against the gstty refere